to this whole other segment.

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:16.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-I mean, TV has its own --

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:20.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, TV has its
own little lane and even --

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:22.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
even when, you know,
we were rolling into the city

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:26.219
yesterday and there's a big
billboard, "American Idol."

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:29.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
And here's this --
this yahoo right here,

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:32.892
and I'm like, "Whoo, all right,
it's about to get interesting."

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:36.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
But Blake was really excited
for me

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:40.834
because he knew it was something
that I would enjoy, and I have.

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:44.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's been -- when I'm on set,
you know, it's been

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:48.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
10, 12-hour days,
but it's fun in this role.

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:49.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm enjoying.
-You have something else

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:50.510 line:92%
really exciting coming up.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:51.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know you're still
going on tour

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:54.147
which is really exciting and
you're playing some stadiums.

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:55.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
-Some baseball stadiums.

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:57.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
Dodger Stadium.
-Dodger Stadium.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:58.585 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-First, is this true?

00:01:58.585 --> 00:02:01.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
The first country music show
ever at Dodger Stadium.

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:04.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
-First country show ever at
Dodger Stadium,

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:07.494
and we're doing -- we're putting
dates up for Fenway.

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:08.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that's exciting.
[ Cheers ]

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:12.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And Wrigley. I was almost
scared that I hadn't announced

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:15.268
all my venues, so I wanted to
keep it secret, but just...

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:16.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-You know,

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:19.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it's been amazing.
We got Sam Hunt out with us.

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:21.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great.
-And Jon Pardi and, uh...

00:02:21.341 --> 00:02:23.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers ]
So it's going to be --

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:25.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's going to be a fun summer.
A lot of fun tailgating

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:28.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
and country music
at Dodger Stadium!

00:02:28.248 --> 00:02:29.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's going to be a first.
-Country music

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:32.051
at Dodger Stadium. Your album is
about how country you are.

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:33.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Is there something --

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:36.623
is there anything you left out?
-On the song --

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:37.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-"What makes you country?"

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:40.226
-Yeah, 'cause, I mean, it tells
a lot of what makes you country?

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:45.665
-Let me see, um, you know, we
have multiple pigs on the farm.

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:47.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. That's good.
That makes you country.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's quite important.
-Yeah.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:52.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have a farm truck that's
used just for the farm.

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:53.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-It doesn't even have

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:54.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
a license plate.
-Oh, wow.

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:56.643 size:81% position:41%
-So you're not allowed
to even drive it on --

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:57.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You can't take it out
on the road.

00:02:57.944 --> 00:02:58.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
-On pavement.
-Yeah.

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:06.319
-And lastly, yeah. I have hired
a full-time bass fishing --

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:08.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I mean, have a guy that --

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:14.460
I have this bass lake and his
job is to grow the bass to --

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:18.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
The biggest bass in the world.
-Wow! And he's full time?

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:21.267
-Full time.
-What does...So what does he do?

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
Does he kind of just go around
with a plate on a boat

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:25.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
and just --
-He hand feeds them.

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:26.306 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-He hand feeds the bass.

00:03:26.306 --> 00:03:29.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, he gives them
massages so they can...swim.

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:31.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-He has a bass spa.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:32.545 size:75% position:38%
-So they can swim --
yeah, the bass spa.

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:36.049
-Gotcha. Now are these --
do these bass get so fat

00:03:36.049 --> 00:03:38.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they're easier to catch?
-Yeah, then they're so --

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:40.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
they're so portly, they don't
really swim well.

00:03:40.687 --> 00:03:42.956
-Yeah. Do you have to even throw
a hook or do you just reach in?

00:03:42.956 --> 00:03:44.958
-So, they're just, like, you
hook them and they're just like,

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:50.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Ahh, I'm tired!"
-[ Laughs ] -"Just end this."

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"It's stressful being
in your pond!"

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:56.102
-That's pretty country. Yeah.
To have a full time bass guy

00:03:56.102 --> 00:03:57.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
is pretty country.
-See, they're all --

00:03:57.237 --> 00:04:00.406
we release them, though, so it's
not like we're growing them for,

00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:04.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
